          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "glog-3a7134ee-3393-4b68-8cd5-34e57b1f31fb",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\n\nThe \"Detected Issue with C Function (malloc)\" vulnerability in C++ arises when the `malloc` function is used improperly, leading to potential memory allocation issues. Specifically, using `malloc(nrow * sizeof(bool))` can be problematic because the size of `bool` is not guaranteed to be 1 byte across all platforms. This can result in incorrect memory allocation, leading to buffer overflows or memory corruption.\n\n### General Mitigation Advice\n\n1. **Use `new` Operator**: Prefer using C++'s `new` operator for memory allocation, which is type-safe and automatically calculates the correct size.\n2. **Check Return Values**: Always check the return value of `malloc` to ensure that memory allocation was successful.\n3. **Use `std::vector`**: Consider using `std::vector` or other standard library containers that manage memory automatically and provide bounds checking.\n4. **Platform-Specific Considerations**: Be aware of platform-specific differences in data type sizes and alignments.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nReplace the `malloc` call with a safer alternative using `std::vector`:\n\n```cpp\n#include <vector>\n\nint main() {\n    size_t nrow = 10; // Example size\n    std::vector<bool> boolArray(nrow);\n\n    // Use boolArray as needed\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n\n### Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following standard library:\n\n- `<vector>`: For using `std::vector`.\n\n### OWASP Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [OWASP Secure Coding Practices](https://owasp.org/www-project-secure-coding-practices-quick-reference-guide/)\n\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\n- [CWE-122: Heap-based Buffer Overflow](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/122.html)\n- [CWE-131: Incorrect Calculation of Buffer Size](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/131.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "DS161085"
                ]
              }
